the maximum number to
stay in that equilibrium.

00:20:51.740 --> 00:20:53.900
So what often happens is
we'll see a population

00:20:53.900 --> 00:20:56.860
actually spike and
overshoot carrying capacity,

00:20:56.860 --> 00:20:59.620
and then we'll see another
kind of mass death event

00:20:59.620 --> 00:21:01.640
and it will get back into equilibrium.

00:21:01.640 --> 00:21:03.910
So it would actually
technically be kind of

00:21:03.910 --> 00:21:06.730
an ecologist's dream to see this happen,

00:21:06.730 --> 00:21:08.750
especially in theory, because we'd be able

00:21:08.750 --> 00:21:11.119
to test out a lot of our theories.

00:21:11.119 --> 00:21:12.700
- So it would overshoot.

00:21:12.700 --> 00:21:14.430
- It would overshoot, yeah.

00:21:14.430 --> 00:21:17.130
My prediction is that depending,

00:21:17.130 --> 00:21:19.180
different species and
different populations

00:21:19.180 --> 00:21:22.420
of organisms would overshoot
at different times.

00:21:22.420 --> 00:21:24.440
So like I'm saying, a deer population,

00:21:24.440 --> 00:21:26.240
herbivores would probably
get there quicker

00:21:26.240 --> 00:21:29.800
than whales or elephants or people, even.

00:21:29.800 --> 00:21:31.694
- And rabbits would get there first.

00:21:31.694 --> 00:21:34.370
(laughter)

00:21:34.370 --> 00:21:35.203
- Exactly.

00:21:35.203 --> 00:21:36.482
- You can bet on that, yeah.

00:21:36.482 --> 00:21:40.840
- But wouldn't you see,
so, I guess that means

00:21:40.840 --> 00:21:44.570
that you would not see the same resulting

00:21:44.570 --> 00:21:48.510
population explosion, or at least...

00:21:48.510 --> 00:21:50.960
- A different mix of animals.

00:21:50.960 --> 00:21:53.410
- Right, because for instance, if you see

00:21:53.410 --> 00:21:57.430
a proliferation of
rabbits or small rodents,

00:21:57.430 --> 00:22:00.400
